### Complex Documentation Patterns

For comprehensive topics, combine multiple components strategically:

## Data Validation :badge[v3.0]{variant="tip"}

{% aside type="note" title="Overview" %}
Data validation ensures input meets requirements before processing. This section covers validation strategies and implementation.
{% /aside %}

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="Schema Validation" %}

{% steps %}
1. **Define Schema**
   
   ```typescript
   const userSchema = {
     name: { type: 'string', required: true },
     email: { type: 'email', required: true },
     age: { type: 'number', min: 0 }
   };
   ```

2. **Validate Input**
   
   ```typescript
   const result = validate(input, userSchema);
   if (!result.valid) {
     throw new ValidationError(result.errors);
   }
   ```

3. **Handle Errors**
   
   {% aside type="tip" %}
   Return specific error messages to help users correct input.
   {% /aside %}
{% /steps %}

{% /tabitem %}

{% tabitem label="Runtime Validation" %}

{% code lang="typescript" title="validator.ts" code="export function validateUser(data: unknown): User {\n  if (!isObject(data)) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid input');\n  }\n  \n  if (!isString(data.name)) {\n    throw new Error('Name must be string');\n  }\n  \n  if (!isValidEmail(data.email)) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid email format');\n  }\n  \n  return data as User;\n}" meta="showLineNumbers mark={6-8,10-12}" /%}

{% aside type="caution" %}
Runtime validation has performance overhead. Use schema validation for better performance.
{% /aside %}

{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

{% collapsible title="Advanced Validation Techniques" %}

{% card title="Custom Validators" icon="puzzle" %}
Create reusable validation functions for complex requirements:

```typescript
const emailValidator = (value: string) => {
  const regex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
  return regex.test(value);
};
```
{% /card %}

{% card title="Async Validation" icon="rocket" %}
Validate against external sources like databases:

```typescript
async function validateUniqueEmail(email: string) {
  const exists = await db.user.findByEmail(email);
  return !exists;
}
```
{% /card %}

{% /collapsible %}

